DocumentLoader.cpp needs EventLoop.h for the type it calls through.

removePlugInStreamLoader() reaches an event loop task group:

    m_frame->protectedDocument()->eventLoop().queueTask(TaskSource::Networking, ...)

`Document::eventLoop()` returns an `EventLoopTaskGroup&`, and calling
queueTask() on it needs the COMPLETE type -- but the file includes no header
that defines one.  ScriptExecutionContext.h, which it does get, carries only
the forward declaration, so the build stops with

    DocumentLoader.cpp:2062:48: error: invalid use of incomplete type
        'class WebCore::EventLoopTaskGroup'

Upstream never sees this because the unified build hides it: WebCore compiles
eight .cpp files per translation unit, and in upstream's default configuration
DocumentLoader.cpp shares its bundle with a file that pulls in EventLoop.h.
Which files land in which bundle depends on the feature flags -- this port
turns off video, web audio, media stream/recorder, WebRTC, encrypted media,
WebGL, WebXR, gamepad and more, so the source list is shorter, the grouping
shifts, and DocumentLoader.cpp comes to sit with neighbours that do not.  The
missing include was always missing; only the neighbour was hiding it.

So the fix is the include the file should have had, in its alphabetical place,
and nothing else -- it is correct in any configuration and does not depend on
which bundle the file lands in.  Same shape as the guard in 0002.

Upstream: not reported yet (latent missing include; candidate for upstreaming).

--- a/Source/WebCore/loader/DocumentLoader.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/loader/DocumentLoader.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
 #include "DocumentWriter.h"
 #include "ElementChildIteratorInlines.h"
 #include "Event.h"
+#include "EventLoop.h"
 #include "EventNames.h"
 #include "ExtensionStyleSheets.h"
 #include "FormSubmission.h"
